## Layer 1: Missing Schema Constraint (Bug Fix)

### Scope Contract
Fix the `Could not fetch list items` crash related to the nonexistent `sortOrder` field. In Sanity Structure Builder, calling `.filter()` completely overwrites the default `_type == "..."` query. Therefore, the expressions `!defined(parent)` and `parent._ref == $parentId` were globally querying ALL documents (including the `hero` schema) instead of being constrained exclusively to `catalogueItem`.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Update the `filter` variable inside `buildCatalogueTree` (around lines 5-7). Prepend `_type == "catalogueItem" && ` to both conditional filter strings.
  Like this:
  `const filter = parentId ? '_type == "catalogueItem" && parent._ref == $parentId' : '_type == "catalogueItem" && !defined(parent)';`
  - Difficulty: 1 - B(sanity/structure.ts): enforce schema boundary on custom VFS filter

### Verification — Layer 1

- [ ] V1.1 — Open Sanity Studio at `http://localhost:3001/studio`. Click the "Catalogue" folder in the sidebar. Confirm it only shows `Headphones`, `Audio Electronics`, and `Accessories` root nodes, and does not crash with ordering config errors.
  - Difficulty: 1

